From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Knox Hutchinson <knox@knoxsdata.com>
Date: Fri, 4 Sep 2026 12:00:00 -0500
Subject: [RFC PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8112-j493: enable SEP for endpoint
 discovery

The M2 MacBook Pro 13-inch (J493) inherits status = "disabled" for the
SEP node from t8112.dtsi and, unlike the M1 laptops t8103-j293 and
t8103-j313, declares no "sep" alias. m1n1's dt_set_sep() only reserves
the SEPFW region and attaches the "sepfw" memory-region plus the
local-policy and iBoot manifests when that alias exists, and the
apple_sep stub refuses to probe without them. Add the alias and enable
the node so the stub binds and the endpoint-advertisement logging from
patch 0001 can record the t8112 inventory.

Test-only: meant for a separately named test kernel on J493, alongside
a stock kernel booted with initcall_blacklist=__apple_sep_init. Not
proposed upstream until the SEP boot result on t8112 is recorded.

Based on Asahi Linux tag asahi-7.1.6-1. The touched hunks are identical
on the asahi branch at 77cb8f24c2381a8abb7272d7bbdec548d6426a8a; only
the trailer line numbers differ.

Signed-off-by: Knox Hutchinson <knox@knoxsdata.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j493.dts | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j493.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j493.dts
index ba237db..dd78bef 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j493.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8112-j493.dts
@@ -25,6 +25,7 @@
 	aliases {
 		bluetooth0 = &bluetooth0;
 		keyboard = &keyboard;
+		sep = &sep;
 		touchbar0 = &touchbar0;
 		wifi0 = &wifi0;
 	};
@@ -331,5 +332,9 @@
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+&sep {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 #include "hwmon-fan.dtsi"
 #include "hwmon-laptop.dtsi"
-- 
